# Variables of the observability stack (PRD-18 RF-14, D-46).
#
# One Dokploy project, shared by staging and production: they are told apart by a label on
# the metrics, not by running two copies of everything.
#
# Its secrets come from a Doppler config of their own -- not from `stg` or `prd`. Those hold
# one environment's JWT keys, database DSNs and broker credentials, and a shared stack
# pointed at either one would need a token that reads all of them to fetch a Grafana
# password. D-33's rule is that a leaked token exposes one config and nothing more, and this
# is the case that would have quietly broken it. RF-15's alert channel belongs here too, for
# the same reason: it is not per-environment either.

# Public hostname of Grafana. Required. It needs an A record pointing at the VPS before the
# first deploy, or Let's Encrypt cannot validate and Traefik serves its default certificate.
#   grafana.v2.dizen.pro
GRAFANA_HOST=

GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=dizen

# SECRET, required. This is the only door into the metrics and traces of BOTH environments,
# and the only component here that is published at all -- Prometheus and Jaeger are not
# routed and have no authentication of their own.
# Generate it with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Traefik certificate resolver, the same one the application projects use.
CERT_RESOLVER=letsencrypt

# --- What the application projects need to be given -------------------------
# Once this is up, OTLP_ENDPOINT in each environment points at Jaeger by container name:
#
#   OTLP_ENDPOINT=dizen-v2-jaeger:4317
#
# Leaving it empty disables exporting rather than retrying against an address that answers
# nothing, so an environment can be brought up before this stack exists.
